// Branch coverage for bls: the package's own tests, and nothing else.
//
//   wac task coverage:bls
//   wac task coverage:bls --verbose
//
// The sixth of the packages `issues/system/0205` records as unmeasured, and the first whose subject is
// a *verifier* rather than a decoder. The five before it were about what an encoding is allowed to
// mean; this one is about which points on a curve a signature check is allowed to accept, and the
// failure it guards against is the same shape one level up — a forged aggregate accepted because some
// guard was never given an input.
//
// **Its own history says the gap is there.** Two of this package's migration commits are titled *"a
// refusal the fixtures do not reach"* and *"which infinity guard is load-bearing"*: someone already
// noticed, in passing, that the vendored vectors do not drive the refusals. Nothing measured how many.
//
// The corpus is the reason to expect it. `verify_test`, `aggregate_test`, `hash_test` and `curve_test`
// are judged against the Ethereum consensus fixtures and the CFRG hash-to-curve vectors — published
// vectors, produced by conforming implementations, containing nothing a conforming implementation
// would never emit. That is the same shape as `rlp`, `mpt`, `ssz` and `abi`, whose corpora are real
// Ethereum data for the same reason and whose canonicity rules were all unexercised.
//
// None of the fifty-three tests expects a trap.

